@model RouteBaseWeb.Models.Sharing.SegmentDetailView
@*
    The segment statistics body, rendered IDENTICALLY by /Segments/Statistics and by the anonymous share
    view at /s/{token}. Two copies would drift, so there is one — gated by Model.Surfaces.

    Adding markup here is free: it appears on both. Adding an OWNER control is not — gate it on
    Model.Surfaces.*, never on Model.IsOwner, because share-ness is a property of the ROUTE (an owner
    opening their own link must see what a stranger sees).

    Partial names are ABSOLUTE on purpose: Razor resolves a partial name against the EXECUTING page's
    directory, so a bare name here would break only on /s/{token}, only at runtime, and dotnet build would
    not catch it. SharedPartialResolutionTests guards this.

    The old `@@if (Model.Segment != null)` guards are gone: SegmentDetailView.Segment is non-nullable, and
    the page 404s before rendering when the segment is not visible. The guards were dead, and keeping them
    would have produced CS8073 "always true" warnings.
*@

<div class="cockpit-scroll">

    <partial name="/Pages/Segments/_SegmentStatsHeader.cshtml" model="Model" />
    <partial name="/Pages/Segments/_SegmentStatsKpis.cshtml" model="Model" />
    <partial name="/Pages/Segments/_SegmentStatsMapPanel.cshtml" model="Model" />
    <partial name="/Pages/Segments/_SegmentStatsCharts.cshtml" model="Model" />
    <partial name="/Pages/Segments/_SegmentStatsEfforts.cshtml" model="Model" />

</div>

<partial name="/Pages/Segments/_SegmentReplayOverlay.cshtml" />
